I come back to my flat.
I sit on the sofa.
I take out my phone.
I always check my calendar.
I look at Saturday's schedule.
I have two tasks on Saturday.
I have a haircut appointment.
This appointment is at eleven o'clock in the morning.
Then I remember Asha's invitation.
The plan for coffee with Asha is also on Saturday.
The coffee time is also at eleven o'clock in the morning.
I look at the phone screen carefully.
Oh no, this is a problem!
Both tasks are at the exact same time.
Haircut and coffee, both are at eleven o'clock in the morning.
I have to change the time of one task.
I definitely want to drink coffee with Asha.
Therefore, I have to change the time of the salon.
I quickly call the salon.
